{ https://youtu.be/6yYOQWfQwCk?si=d5XW283SOToh4oz1&t=2513 } 1. d4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } d5 { [%clk 0:04:57] } 2. Bf4 { [%clk 0:04:58] } e6 { [%clk 0:04:55] } 3. e3 { [%clk 0:04:50] } c6 { [%clk 0:04:51] } 4. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:45] } f5 { [%clk 0:04:50] Completing the pawn chain before bringing out any pieces. } 5. Bd3 { [%clk 0:04:20] } Nf6 { [%clk 0:04:48] } 6. Ne5 { [%clk 0:04:12] Again allowing Ne5. Despite Aman mentioning it was a priority to stop this in an earlier video, in actual fact, he allows it a lot with the black pieces. He often completes the pawn chain before playing Bd6 etc., so if the opponent wants it they can easily get Ne5. The conclusion seems to be that while with the white pieces, Ne4 should be stopped at all costs, with the black pieces, we need to learn to live with it. } Bd6 { [%clk 0:04:46] } 7. Nd2 { [%clk 0:03:54] } O-O { [%clk 0:04:41] } 8. h4 { [%clk 0:03:27] } Qe7 { [%clk 0:04:32] Again readying Nd7. Qc7 also possible. } 9. Bg5 { [%clk 0:03:16] stopping our Ne4 idea. } Nbd7 { [%clk 0:04:27] } (9... h6 10. Ng6 Qf7 11. Nxf8 { h6 here blunders the exchange. }) 10. f4 { [%clk 0:03:05] Playing against the stonewall. } Qe8 { [%clk 0:04:23] breaking the pin. Also covers the g6 square to stop Ng6+ ideas. } 11. Bxf6 { [%clk 0:02:54] } gxf6! { [%clk 0:04:08] Kicking the knight out of e5 } (11... Nxf6 12. Ndf3 { If we take with the knight here, there is just no imbalance to work with. The position is locked up, symmetrical, and drawish. }) 12. Nef3 { [%clk 0:02:36] } Kh8 { [%clk 0:04:03] Taking the time for king safety. Also opens up the g file for offensive operations. } 13. h5 { [%clk 0:02:20] } Rg8 { [%clk 0:03:57] } (13... e5 14. Bxf5 exd4 15. Nf1 dxe3 16. Nh4 e2 17. Qxe2 Qxe2+ 18. Kxe2 Bxf4 19. Re1 Re8+ 20. Kd1 Rxe1+ 21. Kxe1 Ne5 { Engine wanted this kind of continuation. }) 14. Qe2 { [%clk 0:02:12] Our challenge now: how do we get our pieces out? It's going to require some maneuvering. } (14. Nh4 { Engine actually doesn't think much of our position based on this move from white. }) 14... b5 { [%clk 0:03:30] For now, Aman elects to gain some space on the queen side with b and a pawn pushes. } 15. O-O-O { [%clk 0:02:09] } a5 { [%clk 0:03:26] Continuing to gain space. Especially now our opponent has castled right into our pawn storm. } 16. Nh4 { [%clk 0:01:55] Here Aman makes the comment that generally playing against the stonewall, the e5 push is bad, weakening the f pawn, etc., and so is generally to be avoided. } Nb6 { [%clk 0:03:05] switching to QS play. } 17. Rdg1 { [%clk 0:01:46] Looking to push g4, which is strong. } Rg4 { [%clk 0:02:58] stopping g4. } (17... Nc4 18. g4 Rxg4 19. Rxg4 fxg4 20. Qxg4 { We don't want to allow this KS counterplay. }) 18. Qd1 { [%clk 0:01:35] Preparing Be2, but we have Rg3 in that case. } Nc4 { [%clk 0:01:57] } 19. Nxc4 { [%clk 0:01:31] } bxc4 { [%clk 0:01:54] } 20. Be2 { [%clk 0:01:30] } Rg3 { [%clk 0:01:51] A mistake according to the engine. White is better here. } (20... Rxh4 21. Rxh4 Qe7 { According to the engine, this was stronger. }) 21. Qd2 { [%clk 0:01:09] } a4 { [%clk 0:01:09] Sending it. } (21... c3 22. Qxc3 Bxf4 23. Ng6+ hxg6 24. hxg6+ Kg8 25. Bf3 Bd6 { Aman mentioned this tactic was available but it's refuted with best play from the opponent. }) 22. a3 { [%clk 0:01:06] } Rb8 { [%clk 0:01:00] } 23. Rh3 { [%clk 0:01:01] } Rxh3 { [%clk 0:00:47] } 24. gxh3 { [%clk 0:01:01] } Qf8 { [%clk 0:00:40] Keeping an eye on the g8, g7 squares for defense while also eyeballing the a3 pawn with the bishop queen battery. } 25. Qe1?? { [%clk 0:00:57] not stopping our Bxa3 idea. } Bxa3 { [%clk 0:00:23] } 26. bxa3 { [%clk 0:00:47] } Qxa3+ { [%clk 0:00:21] } 27. Kd2 { [%clk 0:00:44] } (27. Kd1 Ba6 28. Qg3 Rb1+ 29. Kd2 c3# { This is what Aman was shooting for. }) 27... Qb4+ { [%clk 0:00:10] } (27... c3+ 28. Kd3 Ba6# { Actually had mate in 2 here. Aman saw it, but was trying for a pawn checkmate as he had a 50sub offer from the live chat if he could manage a pawn mate onstream. }) 28. c3 { [%clk 0:00:42] } Qb2+ { [%clk 0:00:09] } 29. Kd1 { [%clk 0:00:41] } Qb1+ { [%clk 0:00:07] } 30. Kd2 { [%clk 0:00:39] } Qa2+ { [%clk 0:00:07] } 31. Kd1 { [%clk 0:00:36] } Rb2 { [%clk 0:00:05] } 32. Qg3 { [%clk 0:00:31] } Qb1# { [%clk 0:00:01] 0-1 Black wins. Gets the job done with 1 second on the clock. } 0-1

