{ https://youtu.be/LrJH6AeNLCk?si=3sKQ36oBT3SvY1Bo&t=1277 } 1. d4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } d5 { [%clk 0:05:00] } 2. Bf4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } e6 { [%clk 0:04:55] } 3. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:59] } c6 { [%clk 0:04:52] } 4. e3 { [%clk 0:04:58] } Bd6 { [%clk 0:04:49] Again, we conceal our intentions for as long as possible by delaying f5. } 5. Bxd6 { [%clk 0:04:55] } Qxd6 { [%clk 0:04:49] If we see either Nc3 or Bd3 from our opponent we will play f5 } 6. c3 { [%clk 0:04:53] } Nd7 { [%clk 0:04:37] no rush to play f5. keeping our opponent's knight out of e5 } 7. Nbd2 { [%clk 0:04:50] threatening e4 now } f5 { [%clk 0:04:36] just in time to stop e4 } 8. Bd3 { [%clk 0:04:44] } Ngf6 { [%clk 0:04:35] } 9. O-O { [%clk 0:04:25] } O-O { [%clk 0:04:33] } 10. a4 { [%clk 0:04:22] we generally just ignore queenside play } Ne4 { [%clk 0:04:26] } 11. c4 { [%clk 0:04:16] } Rf6 { [%clk 0:03:49] Rh6 or Rg6 ideas } (11... g5 12. Bxe4 fxe4 13. Nxg5 { not good for us }) 12. c5 { [%clk 0:03:37] } Qc7 { [%clk 0:03:26] keeps the knight out of e5 and stays in sight of h2 to potentially line up with the rook in the future if we can get our rook to h6 } (12... Qe7 13. Ne5 Nexc5 14. dxc5 Nxe5 { Qe7 allows Ne5. Technically not a good move as it drops the pawn as per this tactic. But for the purpose of being instructive Aman chose to keep the knight out in the main line. }) 13. b4 { [%clk 0:03:10] "makes sense" } Rh6 { [%clk 0:03:08] e5 push was also an idea. } 14. Ne5 { [%clk 0:03:03] can't do that } Nxe5 { [%clk 0:02:56] } 15. dxe5 { [%clk 0:03:01] } Qxe5 { [%clk 0:02:56] } 16. Nf3 { [%clk 0:02:57] } Qf6 { [%clk 0:02:20] Qc7 was also an option. Aman thought that Qc7 might have been a better short term option but that Qf6 had better long term prospects. i.e. on a strong diagonal, can support g4... g5 can still get to access to the king side. } 17. Bxe4 { [%clk 0:02:40] } fxe4 { [%clk 0:02:16] Aman wishes his queen was on c7 after the opponent takes. } 18. Nd4 { [%clk 0:02:28] } Qh4 { [%clk 0:02:11] } 19. h3 { [%clk 0:02:14] } e5 { [%clk 0:02:10] attacking the knight was uncovering defense of the f5 square and opening up the diagonal to the h pawn. } 20. Ne2 { [%clk 0:01:39] } Bxh3 { [%clk 0:02:08] LSB sack is a common idea to destroy the king's defenses. } 21. gxh3 { [%clk 0:01:34] } Qxh3 { [%clk 0:02:06] } 22. Ng3 { [%clk 0:01:23] } Qh2# { [%clk 0:02:01] 0-1 Black wins. in the post game analysis Aman mentions that the Stonewall is somewhat of an anti-London, in that at the very least you are not allowing the typical London player to set up as they'd like. } 0-1

