{ https://youtu.be/-4n6rkBsF6Y?si=fQOFkAQqcKnP1lj9&t=2499 } 1. e4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } e6 { [%clk 0:04:58] } 2. Bc4 { [%clk 0:04:59] This is the French but generally will lead to the Stonewall as d5 will be almost always met with exd5. } d5 { [%clk 0:04:57] } 3. exd5 { [%clk 0:04:57] } exd5 { [%clk 0:04:56] } 4. Bb3 { [%clk 0:04:55] already good for black. } f5 { [%clk 0:04:53] But not now. The engine actually hates f5 here. Qh5+ is a threat. } (4... Nf6 5. d4 Bd6 6. Nf3 O-O 7. O-O c6 8. Bg5 Bg4 9. h3 Bh5 10. g4 Bg6 11. Ne5 Re8 { How the French exchange may have played out. }) 5. a4 { [%clk 0:04:53] A strange move } (5. Qh5+ g6 6. Qe2+ Be7 7. d4 Nf6 8. Bh6 { we can end up in this kind of messy position. }) 5... Nf6 { [%clk 0:04:51] } 6. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:49] } Bd6 { [%clk 0:04:49] looking nice to complete our setup } 7. d4 { [%clk 0:04:47] } O-O { [%clk 0:04:46] } 8. Bg5 { [%clk 0:04:45] } c6 { [%clk 0:04:34] Important to note that Bg5 pinned the knight so our d pawn is technically hanging here. And we want to play c6 anyway to complete our ideal pawn structure. } (8... Re8+ { This kind of move is actually best but Aman forgoes it in favor of playing the Stonewall. } 9. Kf1 Be6 10. Nc3 c6 11. Ne2 Bf7 12. c3 h6 13. Bf4 Rxe2 14. Bxd6 Re6 15. Bf4 Ne4 16. Ne5 g5 17. Nxf7 Kxf7 18. Bd2 Nd7 19. f3 Nxd2+ 20. Qxd2 Qe7 21. Re1 Re8 22. Rxe6 Qxe6 23. Kf2 Nf6 24. Bc2 Nh5 25. Re1 Qxe1+ 26. Qxe1 Rxe1 27. Kxe1 Ke6 { Interesting line. }) 9. c4 { [%clk 0:04:35] } Re8+ { [%clk 0:04:20] If out opponent isn't going to castle.... } 10. Kd2 { [%clk 0:04:26] a terrible move. What is our opponent thinking? } Ne4+ { [%clk 0:04:18] forking the bishop. } 11. Kc1 { [%clk 0:04:23] } Nxg5 { [%clk 0:04:15] } 12. Nxg5 { [%clk 0:04:17] } Qxg5+ { [%clk 0:04:15] } 13. Nd2 { [%clk 0:04:12] } Be6 { [%clk 0:04:06] } 14. cxd5 { [%clk 0:04:09] } Bxd5 { [%clk 0:04:03] } 15. Bxd5+ { [%clk 0:04:04] } cxd5 { [%clk 0:04:03] } 16. Kc2 { [%clk 0:03:45] } Nc6 { [%clk 0:04:01] one of the few times we'll see Nc6 this speedrun. } 17. Nf3 { [%clk 0:03:41] } Nb4+ { [%clk 0:03:58] } 18. Kb3 { [%clk 0:03:34] } Qe3+ { [%clk 0:03:54] } 19. fxe3 { [%clk 0:03:19] } Rxe3+ { [%clk 0:03:54] } 20. Qd3 { [%clk 0:02:55] } Rxd3# { [%clk 0:03:54] 0-1 Black wins. Disgusting mate. } 0-1

