re. } Nxg3 { [%clk 0:03:15] Aman looked at f4 but "it doesn't do that much after Bh2". } 16. fxg3 { [%clk 0:03:09] } Bxg3 { [%clk 0:03:15] "I got another knight that can go to e4". This wins a pawn, hits the rook. There is a potential discovered on the queen but neither Nxg5??, Qxg5 (bad) or Ne5?! are scary. } 17. Rf1 { [%clk 0:02:59] } Nf6 { [%clk 0:03:01] } 18. Ne5 { [%clk 0:02:57] great looking move, but what is the follow up after we move our queen? } Qh4 { [%clk 0:02:54] } 19. Rxf5 { [%clk 0:02:45] one of the ideas behind moving the knight on d7 to f6 was to uncover the LSB as a defender of this pawn. } Bxf5 { [%clk 0:02:54] } 20. Nd2 { [%clk 0:02:28] } Qxd4+ { [%clk 0:02:50] } 21. Kh1 { [%clk 0:02:23] } Qxe5 { [%clk 0:02:45] opponent is falling apart. } 22. Nf3 { [%clk 0:02:19] } Qf4 { [%clk 0:02:43] We have Ne4 ideas as a follow up. } 23. Qf1 { [%clk 0:02:04] } Ne4 { [%clk 0:02:41] } 24. Nd4 { [%clk 0:01:55] } Nf2+ { [%clk 0:02:39] } 25. Kg1 { [%clk 0:01:52] } Qxd4 { [%clk 0:02:38] 0-1 Black wins. } 0-1

