{ https://youtu.be/NJQGPORLNA0?si=qXpY-NrZFu_58ddt&t=1848 } 1. d4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } d5 { [%clk 0:04:57] } 2. c4 { [%clk 0:04:53] } e6 { [%clk 0:04:50] } 3. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:47] } c6 { [%clk 0:04:45] } 4. Bg5 { [%clk 0:04:43] } f6 { [%clk 0:04:39] Interesting he blocks with f6. } 5. Bh4 { [%clk 0:04:41] } Qb6 { [%clk 0:04:35] Unpins the queen with a threat on the b pawn and prepares f5 next move. Aman uses a similar strategy with the white pieces in order to force the f4 push/ SW structure. } 6. Qc2 { [%clk 0:04:34] } f5 { [%clk 0:04:32] } 7. Nc3 { [%clk 0:04:28] } Be7 { [%clk 0:04:26] Another "non standard" move. Aman doesn't explain why here vs d6. Perhaps white's DSB is too strong and he wants to trade it off? Unfortunately Aman is a bit too into the music at this point in the video, anticipating a drop, and the chess is being played on auto pilot with little commentary. Live by the Chessbrah, die by the Chessbrah. } 8. Bxe7 { [%clk 0:04:25] } Nxe7 { [%clk 0:04:24] } 9. e3 { [%clk 0:04:20] } Nd7 { [%clk 0:04:19] } 10. Bd3 { [%clk 0:04:15] } O-O { [%clk 0:04:16] } 11. O-O { [%clk 0:04:12] } Qd8 { [%clk 0:04:00] } 12. Rfe1 { [%clk 0:04:06] } Ng6 { [%clk 0:03:30] } 13. b4 { [%clk 0:04:01] } Nf6 { [%clk 0:03:28] slowly but surely maneuvering to the king side. Ne4 planned. } 14. a4 { [%clk 0:03:51] } Ne4 { [%clk 0:03:25] } 15. b5 { [%clk 0:03:27] } Bd7 { [%clk 0:03:17] "completing my development". And premoves bxc6 } 16. bxc6 { [%clk 0:03:04] } bxc6 { [%clk 0:03:17] } 17. Reb1 { [%clk 0:02:59] } Qa5 { [%clk 0:02:50] } 18. c5 { [%clk 0:02:38] } Nxc3 { [%clk 0:02:44] "why did he give me this knight here?" } 19. Qd2 { [%clk 0:02:16] "impressed" "he finds a very good move". } Rab8 { [%clk 0:02:38] } 20. Rxb8 { [%clk 0:02:08] } Rxb8 { [%clk 0:02:38] } 21. Rc1 { [%clk 0:02:04] } Rb3 { [%clk 0:02:32] } 22. Bb1 { [%clk 0:01:32] } Qb4 { [%clk 0:02:19] } 23. Ba2 { [%clk 0:01:23] } Rb2 { [%clk 0:02:00] 0-1 Black wins. should be winning another piece here. } 0-1

